    {
      "schema_version": 6,
      "book_id": "MAL",
      "chapter": 2,
      "chapter_usfm": "MAL.2",
      "version_id": 3034,
      "version_abbr": "BSB",
      "verses": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.1",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "“And now this decree is for you, O priests:"
        },
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.2",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "If you do not listen, and if you do not take it to heart to honor My name,” says the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.3",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Behold, I will rebuke your descendants, and I will spread dung on your faces, the waste from your feasts, and you will be carried off with it."
        },
        {
          "verse": 4,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.4",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Then you will know that I have sent you this commandment so that My covenant with Levi may continue,” says the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 5,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.5",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "“My covenant with him was one of life and peace, which I gave to him; it called for reverence, and he revered Me and stood in awe of My name."
        },
        {
          "verse": 6,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.6",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "True instruction was in his mouth, and nothing false was found on his lips. He walked with Me in peace and uprightness, and he turned many from iniquity."
        },
        {
          "verse": 7,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.7",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For the lips of a priest should preserve knowledge, and people should seek instruction from his mouth, because he is the messenger of the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 8,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.8",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But you have departed from the way, and your instruction has caused many to stumble. You have violated the covenant of Levi,” says the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 9,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.9",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "“So I in turn have made you despised and humiliated before all the people, because you have not kept My ways, but have shown partiality in matters of the law.”"
        },
        {
          "verse": 10,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.10",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Do we not all have one Father? Did not one God create us? Why then do we break faith with one another so as to profane the covenant of our fathers?"
        },
        {
          "verse": 11,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.11",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Judah has broken faith; an abomination has been committed in Israel and in Jerusalem. For Judah has profaned the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 12,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.12",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "As for the man who does this, may the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 13,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.13",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "And this is another thing you do: You cover the altar of the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 14,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.14",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Yet you ask, “Why?”It is because the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 15,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.15",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Has not the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 16,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.16",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "“For I hate divorce,” says the Lord says the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 17,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.17",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "You have wearied the LordBy saying, “All who do evil are good in the sight of the Lord"
        }
      ],
      "verse_count": 17,
      "headings": [
        {
          "before_verse": 10,
          "text": "Judah’s Unfaithfulness"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.3",
          "note_ref": "2:3",
          "note_type": "footnote",
          "references": [],
          "text": "Or I will blight your grain"
        },
        {
          "verse": 16,
          "usfm": "MAL.2.16",
          "note_ref": "2:16",
          "note_type": "footnote",
          "references": [],
          "text": "Or “For the man who hates his wife and divorces her,” says the Lord, the God of Israel, “covers his garment with violence,”"
        }
      ],
